  "data": {
    "body": "Four objects, each of mass \\textbf{m} are attached to a disk of mass \\textbf{M} and radius \\textbf{R} as shown. Each object is at distance \\textbf{b} from the axis of the disk. The system is initially at rest on a frictionless flat surface. A string is wound around the disk and such that when the end of the string pulled with a constant force \\textbf{F}, the disks both rotates and translates. When the end of the string is pulled a distance \\textbf{w+d}, the center of mass of the disk (and 4 masses attached to it) has translated a distance  \\textbf{d}.\n\nWhat is the angular speed, $\\omega$ of the system at this instant?\n\nThe moment of inertia $I_{disk}$ = $\\frac{1}{2}MR^2$ and  $I_{pointmass}$ = $mb^2$",
    "solution": [
      0
    ],
    "answerChoices": [
      {
        "id": "c6363962-c901-4d5f-a830-19231623a568",
        "index": 0,
        "body": "$\\omega$ = $\\sqrt{\\frac{4Fw}{8mb^2 + MR^2}}$",
        "questionId": "8453802f-b3e2-494a-8ac3-cc74326d5833",
